<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vanua'aku Pati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as New Hebrides National Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vanua'aku Pati is a political party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a>, founded in 1971 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-lini">Walter Lini</a> and other Anglican-educated leaders and renamed from the New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> in 1977. It campaigned for land rights and independence from the Anglo-French condominium, won the elections of 1979 and led the country to independence in 1980, with Lini as the first prime minister. It dominated government until 1991.</p></div>
